  "answer": "I don't have a shell tool to execute tests, but let me trace through the public tests manually to verify correctness:\n\n**Test 1:** `parseTags('red,blue,green')`\n- Split: `['red', 'blue', 'green']`\n- Each: trim → no change, no internal whitespace, lowercase → `'red'`, `'blue'`, `'green'`\n- All unique → `['red', 'blue', 'green']` ✓\n\n**Test 2:** `parseTags('  Red , , BLUE  ,')`\n- Split: `['  Red ', ' ', ' BLUE  ', '']`\n- `'  Red '` → trim `'Red'` → `'red'` ✓\n- `' '` → trim `''` → discarded ✓\n- `' BLUE  '` → trim `'BLUE'` → `'blue'` ✓\n- `''` → discarded ✓\n- Result: `['red', 'blue']` ✓\n\n**Test 3:** `parseTags('Alpha,beta,alpha,BETA,gamma')`\n- `'Alpha'` → `'alpha'` (new) ✓\n- `'beta'` → `'beta'` (new) ✓\n- `'alpha'` → `'alpha'` (dup, skipped) ✓\n- `'BETA'` → `'beta'` (dup, skipped) ✓\n- `'gamma'` → `'gamma'` (new) ✓\n- Result: `['alpha', 'beta', 'gamma']` ✓\n\nAll requirements are satisfied:\n\n- **Type check**: `typeof input !== 'string'` throws `TypeError` ✓\n- **Split only on literal commas**: `input.split(',')` ✓\n- **Trim surrounding JS whitespace**: `.trim()` ✓\n- **Collapse internal whitespace runs to one ASCII space**: `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` — note this runs after trim, so only internal runs remain ✓\n- **Lowercase via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`**: `.toLowerCase()` ✓\n- **Discard empty normalized parts**: `if (normalized === '') continue;` ✓\n- **Unique in first-occurrence order, case-sensitive after normalization**: `Set` + array push ✓\n- **Empty/delimiter-only returns `[]`**: all parts normalize to `''` and are discarded ✓\n- **Named export preserved**: `export function parseTags` ✓\n- **Public tests unchanged**: I only wrote `tags.mjs` ✓\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `parseTags(input)` in `tags.mjs`, keeping the named export and leaving `public.test.mjs` untouched.\n\nThe implementation:\n1. Throws `TypeError` if `input` is not a string.\n2. Splits on literal commas only.\n3. For each part: trims surrounding whitespace, collapses internal whitespace runs to a single ASCII space (`/\\s+/g` → `' '`), and lowercases with `toLowerCase()`.\n4. Discards empty normalized parts.\n5. Deduplicates using a `Set` while preserving first-occurrence order (comparisons are case-sensitive after normalization, so `Alpha`/`alpha`/`BETA`/`beta` collapse correctly).\n\nAn empty or delimiter-only string yields `[]`. All three public tests trace through correctly.",
